# Redirects for Cloudflare Pages
#
# Intentionally empty. This is a multi-page STATIC Astro build, not a SPA.
#
# The previous "/*  /index.html  200" catch-all was a single-page-app rewrite:
# it served the homepage with HTTP 200 for every path that did not match a
# file, so nonexistent URLs never returned a 404. Search engines treat those
# as soft 404s and index them. Astro already emits a real 404 page and
# Cloudflare Pages serves static assets before consulting this file, so the
# rule bought nothing and cost correct error handling.
#
# The "/portfolio  /portfolio/index.html  200" rule was also redundant —
# Astro emits dist/portfolio/index.html and Pages serves it at /portfolio.
